nizations so it  would be  hypocritical to say that there's nothing  that's going to come  out of it what matters uh i guess and i  think we are  pretty sure about this is that whoever  is the winner in the election uh the  united states will continue to be  a supporter a strong supporter of the  non-proliferation system which is  basically what my organization does and  i i am sure that this is going to be the  case  what about iran there too one gets the  sense that there is a kind of  hiatus at the moment that there's a  waiting period while  the election in the united states takes  place  is there a chance that if donald trump  loses the election there will be a new  impetus to dealing with iran  everybody is is waiting uh for  for the results of of that election um  there will be continuities and there  will be changes there will be  things that will be adapted even with  the same administration or with a new  one  but i think the jcpoa which is this  agreement that germany has been so  supportive of and i was  having a very interesting exchange with  the foreign minister ikomas  about it i think all of this will have  to be looked at  judging the these results but it's not  the only  thing i think there is a lot that the  rest can do on iran of course  as well to see to it that this process  jcpoa or no jcpoa continues in a  constructive  way what's the situation like on the  ground  in iran i mean your inspectors have been  having some trouble there doing their  work on the ground  this year is the situation in danger of  getting out of control is it  particularly dangerous at the moment  well let me say regarding what happened  this year this year was a difficult year  i  i would admit it there were some some  disagreements  between iran and the agency but we were  able to solve this  i think it was important um in short for  those who may not may not be aware  um our inspectors were not allowed to  visit a couple of sites which  which i consider to be very 